  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Winter Energy Needs Supported by Conditional Cash Transfers for Vulnerable Front Line and Other Households in Zaporizhzhia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtWinter is normally a time of hardship for vulnerable communities, and this has been especially exacerbated this year by the continuation of Russian attacks on the energy infrastructure. This has meant that those communities in contested areas are once again highly likely to have power disruptions during the winter months. The proposed project will support the solid fuel heating needs to 4,120 vulnerable households (HHs) in five Hramadas (Matviivska, Mykhalivska, Mykhalivska-Lukasvishka, Pavlivska, and Vilnyanska) in the Zaporizhzia Oblast that are under constant threat and actual attack. Each Hramada Authority nominated HH will receive a one-off conditional cash transfer of USD525 equal to the cost of purchasing locally sourced firewood heating fuel to be delivered to their individual locations (all as per cluster recommendations). The amount purchased is estimated to last the four winter months. This modality has been approved by both the Shelter Cluster and local Hramada Authorities (refer attached letters from each targeted Hramada Authority).ltbrgtThe conditional cash transfer provided by Dorcas will be implemented via UkrPostha (Ukrainian Post Office). ltbrgtIt should be noted that the modality (conditional cash transfer) was successfully implemented last year by Dorcas UA. The only major differences this year is that Dorcas UA is the sole implementer (no Sub IP) and that only UkrPostha will be used (no personal bank accounts. The reason for this is that UkrPostha offers better value for money and no delays due to power outages shutting down local cash machines.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
